{%- comment -%}
  The lunr corpus. One entry per question; assets/js/search.js builds the index
  from this file in the browser (no build step, no npm).

  FIELD CONTRACT — exactly these six keys, in this order:

      qid       "A-1"                    the externally cited question id
      title     "Question A-1: …"        front-matter title, verbatim
      tags      ["42","license"]         always an array
      category  "general"                front-matter category, a single string
      url       "/questions/A-1/"        the permalink
      content   "…"                      answer body, HTML stripped

  WP-E swaps site.posts for the _questions collection here and must not have to
  rename anything — keep the keys and their types stable.

  qid is derived from the permalink rather than stored, because today the front
  matter has no qid field. WP-E adds `qid:` and this becomes `q.qid`.

  post.content may arrive rendered or raw depending on Jekyll's render order,
  so search.js scrubs leftover Liquid/Markdown before indexing (same as docs).
{%- endcomment -%}
[
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
{%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- assign qid_source = post.permalink | default: post.url -%}
{%- assign qid = qid_source | split: '/' | last -%}
{"qid":{{ qid | jsonify }},"title":{{ post.title | jsonify }},"tags":{{ post.tags | jsonify }},"category":{{ post.category | default: '' | jsonify }},"url":{{ post.url | jsonify }},"content":{{ post.content | strip_html | strip_newlines | jsonify }}}
{%- endfor -%}
]
